    {
      "id": "air-basics",
      "title": "Reading the air without panic",
      "tags": [
        "aqi basics reading pm25 who"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "who-2021-aqg",
        "airnow-aqi-basics"
      ],
      "text": "An AQI band tells you how cautious to be, not exactly how you will feel. Use the band with your own plan: who is sensitive, how long you will be outside, and whether you have a filtered room. The WHO 24-hour PM2.5 guideline is 15 micrograms per cubic metre; it is a guideline, not a safe threshold.",
