    {
      "id": "indoor-air",
      "title": "Why indoor air can be worse",
      "tags": [
        "indoor home mass balance cooking windows purifier"
      ],
      "sources": [
        "epa-air-cleaners",
        "epa-ventilation"
      ],
      "text": "Indoor particles come from outside air that leaks in and from sources such as cooking and unflued combustion. A steady-state mass balance is used: outdoor air enters, particles deposit or are removed by a purifier, and indoor sources add mass. A correctly sized purifier and one closed room reduce the space you have to clean.",
